/* The header for this test is at the BOTTOM of this file, below the script.
   It is there because a constant inside a leading comment can swallow the
   rest of the file in the engine - see RMSTEST_56 and the directory README.
   Nothing below the script can do any harm. */

<PLAYER_SETUP>
  grouped_by_team

<LAND_GENERATION>
  base_terrain GRASS

  create_player_lands
  {
    terrain_type GRASS2
    base_size 3
    number_of_tiles 40
    circle_radius 40 0
  }

  create_player_lands
  {
    terrain_type DIRT2
    base_size 2
    number_of_tiles 20
    circle_radius 25 0
  }

<ELEVATION_GENERATION>


<TERRAIN_GENERATION>


<OBJECTS_GENERATION>


<CONNECTION_GENERATION>


/*
================================================================================
RMSTEST_80 - guide:857's documented bug: "with multiple player lands under
grouped_by_team, the additional land positions do not generate properly."
Is it real, and what does "not properly" actually mean?
Feeds: docs/preview-design.md Sec.6.1 line ~245 ("Also emulate guide:857's
bug... " - currently unmeasured, carried as a bare instruction to emulate
something nobody has seen happen), src/preview/generator/lands.ts
================================================================================

THE QUESTION
The guide names a real DE bug and Sec.6.1 currently just says to emulate
it, with no description of what the broken output actually looks like -
there is nothing to emulate FROM. Candidate shapes, all consistent with
"do not generate properly":
  (a) The second command's lands silently collapse onto the FIRST
      command's positions (each player's second land lands exactly where
      their first one did, overlapping).
  (b) The second command's lands ignore grouped_by_team entirely and fall
      back to plain even ring spacing, as if the flag were absent for
      that command only.
  (c) The second command's lands go to originFallbackCenter or some other
      degenerate placement, clustering near the map's true centre
      regardless of team.
  (d) The bug does not reproduce at all under a plain generation (perhaps
      it needs a real multiplayer lobby, or a DE patch already fixed it,
      or the guide's report was itself wrong) - the working model, in
      which case Sec.6.1's "also emulate" instruction should be WITHDRAWN
      rather than carried forward unmeasured, per this project's own rule
      that a shipped map (or a shipped guide claim) is not automatically
      a specification.

METHOD
Two create_player_lands commands under one grouped_by_team <PLAYER_SETUP>.
The first is an ordinary GRASS2 "main" land at radius 40%; the second is a
smaller DIRT2 "extra" land at a different explicit radius (25%) so the two
sets are trivially distinguishable by terrain alone and, if the second set
generates correctly, sit on a visibly different ring. base_size and
number_of_tiles are kept modest (matching RMSTEST_36's own calibration) so
this run tests ONLY the multiple-command question and does not also
trigger RMSTEST_79's separate overflow question.

TEAMS: 2 teams of 4 (players 1-4 vs 5-8), same setup method as RMSTEST_36
and RMSTEST_79.

PREDICTIONS
  WORKS CORRECTLY (guide's bug does not reproduce here, or DE has since
    fixed it) -> both GRASS2 and DIRT2 come back as 8 separate patches
    each, DIRT2's patches team-grouped the same way GRASS2's are (two
    tight clusters of four, ~176-180 degrees apart, matching RMSTEST_36's
    own reading), just on the smaller declared ring.
  MATCHES (a) -> DIRT2 patches sit directly on top of / immediately
    adjacent to GRASS2 patches rather than on their own declared 25%
    ring - fewer than 16 total patches across both terrains, or DIRT2
    patches whose centroids match GRASS2's rather than the smaller
    radius.
  MATCHES (b) -> DIRT2 comes back as 8 patches, but evenly spaced around
    the full ring at roughly 45 degrees apart rather than clustered into
    two team groups the way GRASS2 is.
  MATCHES (c) -> DIRT2 patches (or some of them) cluster near the map's
    true centre, far inside the declared 25% radius, or show
    originFallbackCenter-style collision with other DIRT2 patches.

GENERATE AT NORMAL (200), 8 PLAYERS, 2 TEAMS OF 4. THREE RUNS.

READ WITH
  python probe_scenario.py "<scenario>" --patches GRASS2
  python probe_scenario.py "<scenario>" --patches DIRT2
  Patch count for each terrain first (16 total vs fewer is the headline).
  Then centroids: GRASS2's should reproduce RMSTEST_36's two-cluster
  shape as a sanity check that team grouping is working at all on this
  map; compare DIRT2's shape against it directly.
================================================================================
*/
